identical carat weights but have different length x width measurements depending on the cut. If
you want to choose a smaller carat weight stone, opt for a higher cut grade, as this will make the
stone appear larger. When selecting a stone for a specific budget, try to go slightly under a full
or half carat weight, because prices jump at those sizes. For example, a 1.9ct stone will cost
less than a 2.0ct, and because carat weight is distributed across the entirety of the diamond,
that size difference would be nearly impossible to detect.
